Z||000000||DrRodey||10-16-2000||10:53 AM||||OK Question for all the mega mod guys out there.... I am in need of doing some minor Fiberglassing and can't seem to find anyone who knows anything about it or even where to get the stuff do to it... Any advise or locations would be greatly appreciated.  This something i have been looking at starting for a while but just can't seem to find anyone with the supplies to do it..  HELP PLEASE&gt;&gt;&gt;<P>------------------<BR>'88 Formula CONVERTABLE<BR>'85 Coupe||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-16-2000||11:06 AM||||Check out body shops that do Corvettes.  I know someone who goes to a fiberglass boat builder for modification.  The builder does racing boats and is very good a glass mods.<P>Rather pricy for the boat builder but he gets excellent work done.||||reg||3
Z||000002||2xsess||10-16-2000||11:07 AM||||What exactly are you trying to do? <P>If you have a local body shop you could ask them where they get their supplies or look for a local autobody supply house.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||DrRodey||10-16-2000||11:26 AM||||There are a few parts that i am thinking of adding to my convertable that would require some minor fiberglassing and i wanted to get some supplies to do that and also to practice a little before hand so it doesn't look like udder crap.  Also thinking of some cool ideas for other parts that i can have my gf make molds for, just need the supplies and no one around here knows where to get anything.. ... <P>Already tried the local shops, none of them will tell me where they get their stuff just to bring it in so they can do it and there is no way on Earth i will ever let them touch my baby...<P>------------------<BR>'88 Formula CONVERTABLE<BR>'85 Coupe<BR> <IMG SRC="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/files/smallfc.JPG"> <BR> <A HREF="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html" TARGET=_blank>freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||kinboyatuwo||10-16-2000||11:43 AM||||I don't know about the states but in Canada Canadian tire has all the stuff to get the job done<P>you need the fiberglass material, i think it is called fiberglass resign and the hardner.<BR>instructions are on the box and can.<P>its not too hard takes a little practice but it works<P>||||reg||3
Z||000005||william_thorniii||10-16-2000||12:09 PM||||Dr.Rodney,<P>I have found fiberglassing materials at both Pep Boys and Autozone in Ohio and Michigan.  I reccomend the fine mesh glass mat.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cooter||10-16-2000||02:33 PM||||You cant use fiberglass resin on the Fiero's SMC panels. It will not stay for long! Get SMC panel adhesive.||||reg||1
Z||000007||zeusrekning||10-16-2000||03:55 PM||||my local wal-mart has resin/hardener and fiberglass mat and fiberglass cloth||||reg||1
